course: dictionary
lesson: 8750
title: Setbacks and how to bounce back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A setback is something that stops you moving forward for a while, or makes things harder. The word is made of set and back: it sets you back a step, like a game where you land on a square that moves you backwards.
explain: «The team had a setback when their best player was hurt.» The team did not stop playing, but the injury slowed them down. A setback is a bump in the road, not always the end of the journey.
explain: Setbacks happen to everyone, even the best. In a maths game, «after a setback of 3 points» means you lost 3 points you had. Look at the clues in the sentence: what got worse, and for how long?
fact: Setback means something that stops progress or makes things worse for a while.
fact: Phrases you will meet: suffer a setback, a minor setback, overcome setbacks.
fact: «Stars had setbacks too: as a child Lionel Messi was diagnosed with a growth hormone problem, joined Barcelona at 13 and was helped with his treatment.»
fact: Overcome means you get past something and carry on.
exercise: «The team had a setback when their best player was hurt.» What is a setback? | *Something that slows progress for a while | A long rest after lunch | A kind of sports shoe | A prize for winning the game
exercise: Which phrase means you got past a problem and carried on? | *Overcome setbacks | A minor setback | Suffer a setback | Set back the clock by an hour
exercise: In a maths game, «a setback of 3 points» means what? | *You lose 3 points | You start the game again | You win 3 points | You get a bonus of 3 points
test: What does «a minor setback» mean? | *A small problem that slows you down a little | A long holiday | A huge win | A new bike
test: In a story, the hero loses the map in the forest. What is this? | An ending | A reward | A rest | *A setback
exam: What is the best way to deal with a setback? | Hide it from everyone | Blame the weather | *Learn from it and keep going | Give up for ever
